## Lifecycle and Ownership

Deletion does not cascade; dependent grants and memberships must be removed first. Referencing the identity provider's
namespace orders role creation, but changing that provider under the same namespace requires explicit replacement of
dependent roles.

## Reconciliation

Refresh reads `owner`, `external_id`, and `role_id` from
[SVV_ROLES](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/redshift/latest/dg/r_SVV_ROLES.html); an update runs one `ALTER ROLE`
statement per changed option and re-reads the catalog to verify the result; only a new `name` replaces the role.
`CREATE ROLE` has no owner clause, so creation runs `CREATE ROLE`, with `EXTERNALID` when configured, followed by
`ALTER ROLE ... OWNER TO` for a configured `owner`.

| Change                       | Result                                                                                             |
|------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| `name`                       | replaces the role: the provider never renames a role                                               |
| `owner` set or changed       | `ALTER ROLE ... OWNER TO`, before the external ID                                                  |
| `owner` removed              | no SQL; the current owner stays and is still reported                                              |
| `external_id` set or changed | `ALTER ROLE ... EXTERNALID TO`                                                                     |
| `external_id` removed        | no SQL; the current external ID stays and is still reported, because `ALTER ROLE` cannot remove it |

**Drift.** Refresh compares `SVV_ROLES` with the state, and the next plan sets a configured `owner` or `external_id`
changed outside Terraform back with the statements above; omitted ones follow the catalog and never plan a change. A
role dropped outside Terraform is removed from state and planned for creation. Grants to and from the role are never
read; the grant resources manage them.

